[1] (about=User_2, episodic, t1137 @2025-07-21T18:43:22) I think we need to revisit the coverage plan based on what just came out of validation: the original split — @Ops Lead for cutover, @Change Manager for rollback, with 24x7 handoff — no longer works. The latest run shows the same two Ops engineers are also needed for recon cleanup and access fixes through the freeze window, so live monitoring and after-hours rollback support are now stretched too thin.  

**Proposed change:** put one dedicated support engineer in the war room for the cutover window, and name a delegate to backfill Ops coverage. That keeps monitoring and rollback support separate from cleanup work, which is the cleaner control path here.  

@Ops Lead, please publish the delegate name today; @Support Lead, confirm the war-room assignment in the spec by EOD.
[2] (about=User_3, episodic, t1139 @2025-07-22T01:21:16) Agreed — the coverage split is no longer enough if the same Ops pair are tied up in cleanup. A dedicated war-room engineer plus an Ops delegate gives us cleaner separation, and it protects rollback support from getting buried during recon and access fixes.  

@Ops Lead, please publish the delegate name today, and @Support Lead, confirm the war-room assignment in the spec here: http://sharepoint/treasury_management_system_implementation/risk:_cutover_downtime_spec.

